    G3 REACHABILITY — word against SILENCE on the primary tract, the
       maximum this estimator can attain. A gate that cannot fail cannot
       guard a rejection, so a small value here VOIDS rather than refuses.
       IT ALSO SELECTS THE ESTIMATOR, on this label-independent contrast
       alone and never on /a/-vs-/i/.

       /a/ vs SILENCE  a magnitude contrast -- NOT an upper bound, see §68
         d' POOLED over B   (registered)     0.4425 +- 0.0069   does NOT clear
         d' drive RATIO     (addendum)        1.4649 +- 0.0228   clears
         d' WITHIN B        (addendum)        0.7379 +- 0.0256   does NOT clear
       -> NOT A VALID POSITIVE CONTROL. Silence differs from a word in
          MAGNITUDE; two vowels differ in PATTERN, and this statistic is
          pattern-sensitive. The cascade shows silence is the HARDER
          contrast, so this pair cannot bound anything and VOIDS NOTHING.
          Its guard role passes to the arithmetic clause, which has a
          provable bound (U <= 1). Kept as a stimulus-ladder rung.

